{
  "title": "SIRI adds no robust cross-cycle CRP prediction beyond flexible blood-count and ratio models",
  "abstract": "In 4,122 source and 4,927 target NHANES adults, adding the systemic inflammation response index (SIRI) increased target log-CRP MSE by 0.000754 (0.070%). The source-refit/target-PSU 95% interval spans benefit and harm. Small source cross-validation gains did not transport reliably; this is exploratory same-program temporal validation, not an untouched external cohort.",
  "keywords": [
    "SIRI",
    "CRP",
    "NHANES",
    "incremental prediction",
    "negative result"
  ],
